WEBVTT

00:00:01.542 --> 00:00:04.503
<i>Hot in Cleveland is recorded
in front of a live studio audience.</i>

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.962
The strangest thing
just happened to me.

00:00:07.087 --> 00:00:09.398
I had a conversation
with a neighbor.

00:00:11.873 --> 00:00:14.038
I never even saw
my neighbors in L.A.

00:00:14.163 --> 00:00:15.931
Except during earthquakes.

00:00:17.518 --> 00:00:20.363
Sometimes we'd pull out
of our driveways at the same time

00:00:20.488 --> 00:00:22.738
and as our electronic gates
were opening,

00:00:22.863 --> 00:00:25.678
I don't even know their names,
and they don't know mine.

00:00:25.803 --> 00:00:27.414
And the world was good.

00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:31.951
That was the L.A. us.

00:00:32.076 --> 00:00:34.520
Here, we're gonna get to know
our neighbors.

00:00:34.645 --> 00:00:36.018
I'm throwing a party.

00:00:36.143 --> 00:00:39.162
Tomorrow.
Look at me being all spontaneous.

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:52.940
I changed my hair.

00:00:56.849 --> 00:00:57.879
Why would...

00:00:59.477 --> 00:01:00.712
I mean, why?

00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:03.785
I wanted something fresh.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:07.482
I found a picture in a magazine,
and I gave it to my hair stylist.

00:01:08.164 --> 00:01:09.929
Was it a picture of Elmo?

00:01:12.974 --> 00:01:15.328
This red hair comes with a temper.

00:01:15.453 --> 00:01:16.741
I will cut you.

00:01:19.064 --> 00:01:21.080
Okay, red, what's going on?

00:01:21.376 --> 00:01:24.328
Max invited me
to the senior senior prom.

00:01:26.523 --> 00:01:28.057
That is so cute.

00:01:28.182 --> 00:01:29.647
Yeah, if you think...

00:01:29.772 --> 00:01:32.758
piranhas surrounding
a baby seal is cute.

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:36.499
So the ladies love Max, huh?

00:01:36.624 --> 00:01:38.782
Especially Agnes Bratford.

00:01:38.907 --> 00:01:41.638
Or should I say fat-ass hag-ford.

00:01:46.788 --> 00:01:48.922
She doesn't sound
like much of a rival.

00:01:49.047 --> 00:01:51.116
She takes hormone replacements.

00:01:51.963 --> 00:01:54.321
I can't compete with
someone who's doping.

00:01:55.536 --> 00:01:57.351
I have to take it up a notch.

00:01:58.293 --> 00:02:01.078
Now I just need the dress
to make it all pop.

00:02:01.878 --> 00:02:04.442
Don't forget the red
nose and floppy shoes.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.154
<i>Oh, my God.
Is that Victoria Chase?</i>

00:02:12.279 --> 00:02:13.299
New ringtone?

00:02:13.552 --> 00:02:14.778
Don't judge.

00:02:17.156 --> 00:02:19.250
- <i>Victoria Chase?</i>
- It's my Agent.

00:02:19.375 --> 00:02:22.593
He sent a text, but I can't read it.
My glasses are upstairs.

00:02:22.718 --> 00:02:24.100
No, a little further.

00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:25.839
Good, good.

00:02:25.964 --> 00:02:29.043
A Japanese company wants
me to do a commercial.

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:33.401
Years of honing my craft,
and finally my dream is coming true.

00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:36.296
Your dream is to do a
Japanese commercial?

00:02:37.003 --> 00:02:39.699
To sell out
for an obscene amount of money.

00:02:40.347 --> 00:02:41.596
What's the product?

00:02:41.721 --> 00:02:43.036
I'm not sure.

00:02:43.357 --> 00:02:45.507
Beneficial dryness force.

00:02:46.371 --> 00:02:48.375
Probably some sort
of antiperspirant.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.928
That's not so bad.
A lot of a-listers do it.

00:02:51.053 --> 00:02:54.390
I heard Brad Pitt did a Japanese
commercial for baby formula.

00:02:54.515 --> 00:02:57.282
I know, and now nutrition
breast juice wow

00:02:57.407 --> 00:02:59.511
is, like, the number one brand.

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:02.973
You never told us
what your senior prom theme was.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.963
Let me guess...
a night to try to remember?

00:03:14.866 --> 00:03:16.560
Let's play a game.

00:03:17.499 --> 00:03:20.365
Raise your hand if
you've got a boyfriend.

00:03:23.578 --> 00:03:26.160
Hot In Cleveland
1x05 - Good Neighbors

00:03:26.285 --> 00:03:28.700
Hot In Tracksuit
Team

00:03:28.825 --> 00:03:31.377
Logdo, Skualler
Sososeries et Thirteen.

00:03:32.243 --> 00:03:34.059
- Cupcakes are up.
- Actually,

00:03:34.184 --> 00:03:35.523
they're Ohio cakes.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:38.425
'cause they're round on the ends
and high in the middle.

00:03:38.745 --> 00:03:40.608
Get it? O-hi-o.

00:03:42.895 --> 00:03:45.598
Are you sure you're not
high in the middle?

00:03:45.966 --> 00:03:47.911
I just want to make
a good impression.

00:03:48.036 --> 00:03:49.564
I got great Lake Latkes.

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:51.347
And I have drew curry

00:03:52.055 --> 00:03:53.439
with Lebron rice.

00:03:53.564 --> 00:03:55.235
And to wash it all down,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.850
some cold, delicious
Cuyahoga River punch.

00:03:57.975 --> 00:04:01.032
That River was so polluted,
it actually caught fire once.

00:04:01.157 --> 00:04:02.557
But they cleaned it all up.

00:04:02.682 --> 00:04:05.537
Some of us happen
to like a little pollution.

00:04:09.526 --> 00:04:11.566
My agent just sent a box of...

00:04:12.004 --> 00:04:13.826
ozawa industrial brothers

00:04:13.951 --> 00:04:16.297
Mrs. Ladypant beneficial
dryness force.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:22.052
Mrs. Ladypants. I'm thinking
it's not an antiperspirant.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.674
"Say greeting to Mrs. Ladypant.

00:04:24.799 --> 00:04:27.004
For best good times, be on dry."

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.238
That's weird.

00:04:32.363 --> 00:04:34.794
There's, like, something in there.
Like a...

00:04:34.919 --> 00:04:36.111
a pad or...

00:04:37.219 --> 00:04:38.235
A diaper.

00:04:40.984 --> 00:04:43.782
What are you talking about?
They're pants.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.942
With an attractive inner padding.

00:04:48.145 --> 00:04:49.381
On their butt.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:51.966
Give it up.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.024
- It's a diaper.
- It's not a diaper!

00:04:54.149 --> 00:04:55.307
It's pants.

00:04:55.432 --> 00:04:59.034
And they're comfortable
and perfectly stylish, and I love them.

00:04:59.159 --> 00:05:01.549
And they are paying me
a ton of money to...

00:05:01.843 --> 00:05:02.955
"Preserve...

00:05:03.671 --> 00:05:05.271
Freshness of crotch."

00:05:09.463 --> 00:05:10.597
As pants do.

00:05:11.307 --> 00:05:12.602
So just lay off.

00:05:19.286 --> 00:05:22.177
Isn't this great? Look how happy
and relaxed everyone is.

00:05:22.302 --> 00:05:25.517
I know. In L.A., by now, I'd have had
at least one conversation

00:05:25.642 --> 00:05:28.841
where someone's looking past me
to find someone more important.

00:05:28.966 --> 00:05:30.320
Yeah, I hate that.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:36.765
And don't you just love
how everyone seems to have worn

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:37.962
whatever?

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.518
Look at those women.
Their hair is still wet.

00:05:40.643 --> 00:05:43.063
It took me an hour and a half
to blow this dry.

00:05:43.188 --> 00:05:45.446
Maybe we should take
a lesson from them.

00:05:45.918 --> 00:05:48.274
Or maybe they could take
a blow dryer from us.

00:05:48.399 --> 00:05:50.148
- Hello, ladies.
- Hello.

00:05:50.273 --> 00:05:52.130
I'm Rick from across the street.

00:05:52.255 --> 00:05:54.216
And, yes, I do smell of fish.

00:05:57.691 --> 00:05:59.316
We weren't gonna say anything.

00:05:59.571 --> 00:06:02.389
I just had a glorious morning
fishing on Lake Erie.

00:06:02.514 --> 00:06:04.424
I could bring you
some muskie some time.

00:06:04.549 --> 00:06:06.292
What a lovely offer.

00:06:06.417 --> 00:06:08.116
There's that fish smell.

00:06:09.774 --> 00:06:13.619
- So are you a fisherman?
- No, I work for the plain dealer.

00:06:13.744 --> 00:06:17.137
I write a column on Cleveland,
what I like, what I don't like.

00:06:17.262 --> 00:06:19.446
What I would like is
to interview you, Melanie.

00:06:19.571 --> 00:06:22.029
It's quite a thing
to get a best-selling author.

00:06:22.154 --> 00:06:24.666
And a famous actress.
Crazy, huh?

00:06:25.986 --> 00:06:28.311
I'm not really an author.
One book.

00:06:28.436 --> 00:06:30.843
Jotted down 200 things
I wanted to do one day.

00:06:30.968 --> 00:06:32.745
But it did sell like crazy.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:35.207
Although it wasn't on
television for 27 years.

00:06:37.195 --> 00:06:39.308
Let her or I'll tell him
about your diapers.

00:06:39.433 --> 00:06:40.825
- Pants.
- Diapers.

00:06:42.652 --> 00:06:45.154
So was moving to Cleveland
one of your list things?

00:06:47.035 --> 00:06:50.867
Before I came here, I thought, Cleveland
was one of those places people came from

00:06:51.035 --> 00:06:52.472
but they never went to.

00:06:53.387 --> 00:06:56.206
So what made you choose
Cleveland over L.A.?

00:06:56.426 --> 00:06:58.363
Gosh, where do I start?

00:06:59.164 --> 00:07:01.885
In L.A.,
everyone is so thin and perfect.

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.292
It really starts to mess
with your self-esteem.

00:07:04.417 --> 00:07:06.092
But here, I feel great.

00:07:09.944 --> 00:07:10.949
I see.

00:07:11.223 --> 00:07:13.888
Wait. I think I'm not
communicating very well.

00:07:14.142 --> 00:07:16.247
You know,
Melanie isn't as accustomed

00:07:16.372 --> 00:07:18.392
to being interviewed as I am.

00:07:18.517 --> 00:07:20.693
You could just
let her have a few moments

00:07:20.818 --> 00:07:23.345
to gather her thoughts and
go grab something to eat?

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:25.944
Right, why don't I just go
feed my fat, ugly face.

00:07:26.196 --> 00:07:27.612
You forgot smelly.

00:07:31.754 --> 00:07:34.093
What is wrong with me?
How did that happen?

00:07:34.218 --> 00:07:37.034
I meant to say that people in L.A.
are vain and superficial.

00:07:37.159 --> 00:07:38.955
- I got to fix this.
- Just let it go.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.315
You try to fix that,
you will only make it worse.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.759
But he's our neighbor.

00:07:42.884 --> 00:07:45.373
And a columnist.
I don't want him not to like me.

00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:47.397
I like being likeable.

00:07:47.522 --> 00:07:49.889
Not to brag,
but it's kind of my thing.

00:07:50.366 --> 00:07:52.995
You should be able to tolerate
someone not liking you.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:56.697
You're right. A ton of people
don't like you, and you're fine with it.

00:07:58.853 --> 00:08:00.817
I'm gonna staple my mouth shut.

00:08:00.942 --> 00:08:02.429
As soon as I fix this.

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:05.777
I'm just... I'm sorry.

00:08:05.902 --> 00:08:07.443
I'd like to explain.

00:08:07.696 --> 00:08:10.247
When I said that people in L.A.

00:08:10.372 --> 00:08:11.792
are perfect and thin,

00:08:11.917 --> 00:08:14.941
I did not mean to imply that
everyone here is fat and ugly.

00:08:15.654 --> 00:08:18.520
I just mean, people in L.A.,
they're abnormally thin.

00:08:18.645 --> 00:08:20.645
Right? Everyone here is normal.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.083
They're healthy.

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:24.470
I don't know if I would use healthy.

00:08:24.595 --> 00:08:26.988
'Cause, there have
been studies, and it's ver...

00:08:27.787 --> 00:08:29.741
What I mean to say is that,

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:33.095
here, you can relax, you know,
and let yourself go.

00:08:36.141 --> 00:08:39.560
You see it happening, but there's
nothing you can do about it.

00:08:39.728 --> 00:08:42.441
So you think we've let ourselves go.

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:44.936
I meant that, here,

00:08:45.563 --> 00:08:46.754
life is simpler.

00:08:46.879 --> 00:08:48.619
It's like going back in time.

00:08:48.744 --> 00:08:50.028
So we're backward.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:53.907
Why aren't you understanding this?

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:55.814
Just simple, I guess.

00:08:56.758 --> 00:08:58.446
I was wrong. She fixed it.

00:08:59.664 --> 00:09:02.999
How about we all have
some Cuyahoga River punch?

00:09:06.741 --> 00:09:09.139
That River hasn't caught
fire in 40 years.

00:09:09.264 --> 00:09:12.331
- I'm sorry. Let me explain.
- Oh, no, that's all right.

00:09:12.456 --> 00:09:13.910
I got a column to write.

00:09:14.035 --> 00:09:17.513
No, I love Cleveland. I love Lebron.
Or I don't. You tell me!

00:09:17.766 --> 00:09:20.643
Frankly, you guys are a little
wishy-washy on that one.

00:09:23.188 --> 00:09:25.817
- It's a fabulous party.
- Really.

00:09:29.499 --> 00:09:31.862
- What am I gonna do?
- Stop worrying so much.

00:09:32.231 --> 00:09:35.310
Cleveland's a rock and roll town.
Lots of party end with fire.

00:09:37.118 --> 00:09:39.709
I can't help but worry,
'cause if Rick is writing the article

00:09:39.834 --> 00:09:42.570
I think he's writing about me,
the whole city's gonna hate me.

00:09:42.695 --> 00:09:44.703
Just leave it alone.
It'll blow over.

00:09:45.746 --> 00:09:48.434
I know what I have to do.
I have to go across the street

00:09:48.559 --> 00:09:49.791
and talk to him.

00:09:49.916 --> 00:09:53.217
And he'll see that I'm a nice person,
because he's a nice person, right?

00:09:53.385 --> 00:09:56.428
Because your plan has
worked so well up to this point.

00:09:56.596 --> 00:09:59.339
That's why you're gonna
come over there and back me up.

00:09:59.464 --> 00:10:00.717
Why do I have to?

00:10:00.842 --> 00:10:03.769
You're the one who went all
Don Rickles on Cleveland.

00:10:09.526 --> 00:10:11.823
Where's Victoria?
I'm gonna need her too.

00:10:11.948 --> 00:10:13.570
Upstairs, trying on her pants.

00:10:16.336 --> 00:10:18.366
I don't think we want
to interrupt that.

00:10:20.972 --> 00:10:24.053
Do you think he'll like the wine?
Or does it seem pretentious?

00:10:24.178 --> 00:10:26.792
Should I have brought beer?
Or is that insulting?

00:10:26.917 --> 00:10:30.087
God, is this from California?
Do they make Cleveland wine?

00:10:30.255 --> 00:10:33.150
What did we say about too
many questions in a row?

00:10:33.275 --> 00:10:35.063
I'm doing it again, aren't I?

00:10:35.188 --> 00:10:38.262
What's wrong with me?
What is it with me and questions?

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:41.755
- He's not home. We'll try again later.
- Wait, no. I see his computer.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:45.227
It's got writing on it. It says,
"Melanie MoRetti is a horrible person."

00:10:45.746 --> 00:10:48.317
- How can you read that from here?
- I just know.

00:10:48.442 --> 00:10:51.312
- We have to sneak in and read it.
- What?

00:10:51.437 --> 00:10:53.825
Don't you see?
If it's not bad,

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:55.775
then I'll just relax. But...

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.395
if it's terrible,

00:10:57.688 --> 00:11:00.562
someone who really cares
about me could delete it.

00:11:01.925 --> 00:11:03.854
Wait. What's that noise?

00:11:18.923 --> 00:11:20.936
I can't believe you left without me.

00:11:21.061 --> 00:11:22.922
Are you wearing your diaper pants?

00:11:23.752 --> 00:11:27.436
Stop saying that. It is the
Mrs. Ladypant beneficial dryness force.

00:11:29.147 --> 00:11:31.861
I have to wear it at least
once before I can legally say,

00:11:31.986 --> 00:11:33.900
"I feel as fresh as mt. Fuji."

00:11:36.779 --> 00:11:38.405
Are we breaking into or what?

00:11:38.573 --> 00:11:40.591
You don't even know
why we're breaking in.

00:11:40.716 --> 00:11:43.226
I'm assuming it's either
to read his column or delete it.

00:11:43.351 --> 00:11:44.702
- See?
- All right.

00:11:44.827 --> 00:11:46.942
Wait, you go first.
You have padding.

00:11:51.294 --> 00:11:53.217
God, I can't look.
What's it say?

00:11:53.342 --> 00:11:54.971
- Oh, my God.
- What?

00:11:55.096 --> 00:11:56.438
What? Is it bad?

00:11:56.932 --> 00:11:59.651
It's terrible.
He doesn't even mention me.

00:12:01.513 --> 00:12:05.098
It's not bad at all.
He just says I'm a well-meaning klutz.

00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:08.445
I guess that trumps
award-nominated actress.

00:12:09.229 --> 00:12:10.646
I am so relieved.

00:12:11.356 --> 00:12:14.191
- Then what are you doing?
- Changing my age, of course.

00:12:14.359 --> 00:12:15.317
Let's go.

00:12:15.485 --> 00:12:17.049
And don't leave any smudges.

00:12:17.174 --> 00:12:19.213
I don't want him to know
anybody's been here.

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:22.074
Wait, I can still get away with 41.

00:12:27.664 --> 00:12:30.490
I can't believe we just did that.
My heart is still pounding.

00:12:30.615 --> 00:12:33.119
I haven't felt this excited
about getting away with something

00:12:33.244 --> 00:12:36.580
since I convinced my fourth husband
that I was still a virgin.

00:12:36.925 --> 00:12:38.484
That was some acting.

00:12:39.417 --> 00:12:41.760
I say that we celebrate
now that it's all over.

00:12:41.885 --> 00:12:44.958
How about we open that bottle of wine
you were gonna give to Rick?

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:48.927
- Something else.
- No. I mean, it's still there.

00:12:49.052 --> 00:12:52.187
I forgot to bring it out with me,
and it's got a note on it from me.

00:12:52.355 --> 00:12:55.389
- He's gonna know I was there.
- Great. We better hurry.

00:12:59.134 --> 00:13:00.540
You make too much noise.

00:13:00.665 --> 00:13:04.275
Just text me if you see him coming.
I'll be right back.

00:13:05.681 --> 00:13:07.411
Hi, Elka. Is that your dress?

00:13:07.713 --> 00:13:09.413
Don't start with me.

00:13:10.087 --> 00:13:12.457
- What's wrong?
- My hair.

00:13:13.258 --> 00:13:16.267
I got a good look at myself
in the dress shop.

00:13:16.392 --> 00:13:18.616
I look like little orphan granny.

00:13:19.528 --> 00:13:21.550
Why didn't you say something?

00:13:21.718 --> 00:13:24.018
To be fair,
I did say you looked like Elmo,

00:13:24.143 --> 00:13:26.946
and I had a couple of good
bozo jokes at the ready too.

00:13:28.539 --> 00:13:31.143
I'm not gonna even go
to that stupid prom.

00:13:31.311 --> 00:13:33.687
All the cool seniors
stay home anyway.

00:13:35.892 --> 00:13:37.858
Get back here, raggedy Ann.

00:13:39.225 --> 00:13:40.311
Last one.

00:13:41.746 --> 00:13:45.699
I'm not just an eyebrow expert. I'm good
with all kinds of unwanted hair.

00:13:47.484 --> 00:13:49.161
I can help you.

00:13:49.329 --> 00:13:52.122
You're in cahoots with
fat-ass hag-ford, aren't you?

00:13:54.572 --> 00:13:58.407
Now you may not realize this, Elka,
but we are in the presence of a genius.

00:13:59.194 --> 00:14:01.988
Ill-tempered,
disagreeable, snarky, yes. But...

00:14:03.009 --> 00:14:06.628
I would trust her with my life,
and more importantly, with my hair.

00:14:08.333 --> 00:14:10.392
I know we can be hard on each other,

00:14:10.517 --> 00:14:11.975
but you have my word.

00:14:12.273 --> 00:14:14.600
I will do whatever I can with...

00:14:14.725 --> 00:14:15.736
... that.

